  "term": "pituitary adenoma",
  "definition": "A pituitary adenoma is a well-differentiated neuroendocrine tumor that develops from hormone-producing cells in the front part of the pituitary gland. It may produce hormones or be nonfunctioning, and it only rarely spreads to other parts of the body.",
